॰ THE ARGUMENT TAGS ARE DECLARED AND NEVER READ. yantra places the arguments by scanning
॰ RAM AFTER the input is placed, so when the input image is itself a .t1 program that
॰ reads arguments, its tags are found inside the input's copy and yantra patches the
॰ copy — the translated image would then carry yantra's pointer instead of its own
॰ octets. Declaring them here makes such a tag occur twice, and yantra hands over no
॰ arguments at all (measured: hello.elf's image differed in 5 octets until this).
सार्वजनिक चरः आदेशसङ्केतः ॱॱ न६४ भवति २४२८५२६६६०५९८२०३५ ।
