॰ ARG0 (what the program will see as argument 0) arrives as the input's name run.
॰ NOT AS AN ARGUMENT: yantra finds the argument slots by scanning RAM after the input
॰ is placed, so an input image that itself declares the argument tags (every .t1
॰ program that reads its arguments) makes the tag occur twice and the arguments are
॰ refused. The name run is placed with the input, from the tag found before it.
